// endpoint_get_peer_recipient.proto — GetPeerRecipient: WHICH SESSION received
// one cross-session message, by the vendor's delivery id for it.
//
// WHY ANYONE ASKS. A send to another Claude session names its recipient only
// as the address the caller wrote, and the one value both ends share is the
// delivery id the sending vendor minted (conversation.v1.PeerDeliveryId): the
// sender's SendMessage result carries it, and so does the recipient's record of
// the message. The daemon draws the sender's row and wants to name the session
// the message reached; on a live delivery it sees the recipient's record land,
// but a send replayed from history needs the record's owner from the record.
//
// WHY THE STORE CAN ANSWER. Every session on the host writes into this one
// store, so the recipient's record is here whichever session holds it, keyed by
// its delivery id at write time (PeerMessageInterSession.delivery_id).
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT SCOPED TO THE CALLER'S LINEAGE, unlike GetLiveWork and
// GetAgentByVendorTask: the question is which OTHER session holds a record, so
// a lineage scope would refuse every answer the endpoint exists to give. The
// answer is one agent id, never the record's content.

